  "reason": "Subagent lifecycle fixes (LIVE-3, SUB-5, SUB-6, SUB-8, SUB-9, SUB-10, SUB-12, GOAL-5). The new tests/v3/test_chat_subagent_lifecycle.py pins each rule: failed/stopped parents stop their children with a reason (completed, retryable-answer and restart-interrupted parents keep them; harness failures too), Stop during a next-round start leaves nothing running, approval-blocked children are released when the supervisor ends, rewind retracts the edited exchange's subagents (service and API route), children inherit exactly the parent's SSH hosts at start and on later rounds, goal continuation reuses turn_settings and treats a lost race as expected, goal token budgets bound children as they spend with idempotent true-up charges, and goal active time excludes idle gaps and reports the open stretch once. The other files cover the changed paths: subagent start/stop/rounds/delivery/restart (test_chat_subagents, harness provider subagents, subagent choice), goal lifecycle/budgets/read and schedules turn_settings/SSH filtering (test_chat_goals, test_chat_schedules, test_ssh_environments), provider turn claim/release/stop/rewind/budget fitting in the chat service, tool loop and final-answer recovery (test_chat, test_chat_api, test_chat_tool_loop, test_chat_final_synthesis_recovery, test_routing_prose_answer, test_reasoning_recovery, test_turn_outcome_history) and agent messaging delivery (test_chat_agent_messages).",
  "exclusions": "Full suites are not approved and are excluded. Individual node ids replace whole files for test_chat_subagents.py (14 nodes), test_harness_provider_subagents.py (3), test_chat.py (22), test_chat_api.py (4) and test_chat_final_synthesis_recovery.py (1): those 44 nodes fail identically on pristine origin/main (4facf4a and eadae6a) (the #559 admission and #521 output-limit regressions that claude/resume-admission and others are fixing) and fail the same way with this change; they are re-added when this branch rebases onto those fixes. test_model_output_budget.py (15 of its nodes red on main) covers default output sizing, which this change does not touch. No frontend, Playwright or native code changed; the UI reads the same goal fields (elapsed_seconds/active_since) and no controls or layouts changed. Real-Core evidence is recorded in the PR.",
